// Signing, kept out of the project file.
//
// `DEVELOPMENT_TEAM` is a property of the machine building the app, not of the
// app. With it stored in `project.pbxproj`, Xcode rewrote it to whichever team
// the current developer had, every checkout produced a spurious diff, and
// committing one meant the other developer's build failed with "No Account for
// Team".
//
// So the project reads `$(COVE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM)` instead, and each machine
// supplies it from `Signing.local.xcconfig` — which is ignored by git and never
// leaves the Mac that made it.
//
// To set yours up:
//
//     echo 'COVE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = YOURTEAMID' > Config/Signing.local.xcconfig
//
// Your team id is in Xcode → Settings → Accounts, or on the Apple Developer
// site under Membership.

// Optional on purpose: a fresh clone builds without one. Signing is what fails
// then, and it fails saying so, rather than the project refusing to open.
#include? "Signing.local.xcconfig"

// Left empty when no local file supplies it.
COVE_DEVELOPMENT_TEAM = $(inherited)
